    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **262 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created (`POST /api/owners`), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `AddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 the single source of truth for canonical address form: trim, collapse internal whitespace to one space, upper-case, and expand whole-token street abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). A null/whitespace-only input normalizes to `\"\"`. Expansion matches only whole space-delimited tokens, so `\"st.\"` (trailing period) and substrings are left alone.\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that writes the normalized address back onto the request, so it's what gets stored and returned.\n\n**Changed files:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 wired `normalizeAddress` into the pipeline after `normalizeEmail` and before the household checks (under the same `transaction` governance).\n- `ValidateOwner.java` \u2014 the required-field check now rejects an address that is blank *after* normalization.\n- `EnsureOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` and `AssignHouseholdId.java` \u2014 the address side of the household duplicate-detection comparison and the shared household-id derivation now use `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` on both the request and existing owners, so comparisons use the normalized form regardless of pipeline order (existing/seed owners get normalized on the fly).\n\nThe update path (`PUT`) is intentionally untouched for storing, since the spec scopes normalization to owner *creation*; `ValidateOwner` is shared, so PUT also gains the blank-after-normalization rejection, which is consistent and harmless for valid addresses.\n\nAll three new acceptance tests pass (whitespace/case normalization \u2192 `12 MAIN STREET`, abbreviation expansion \u2192 `7 ELM AVENUE`, and blank-after-normalize \u2192 400), along with the existing household duplicate-detection tests.",
